summary:
The paper aims to present new results on the boundedness of Bergman type projections in tubular domains over irreducible symmetric cones and in products of such domains, noting that some parameter cases are already known. It introduces basic notation and definitions for complex function theory on tube domains over symmetric cones, including the tube domain \(T\Omega = V + i\Omega\), holomorphic function spaces \(H(T\Omega)\), the rank \(r\) of the cone, and the determinant function \(\Delta\). It defines weighted analytic function spaces \(A_{\infty}^{	au}(T\Omega)\) and mixed-norm weighted Bergman spaces \(A_{
u}^{p,q}(T\Omega)\), states that \(A_{
u}^{p,q}(T\Omega)\) is nontrivial iff \(
u>-1\), and gives the Bergman projection \(P_
u\) along with its integral representation using the Bergman reproducing kernel. The paper also discusses a second part focused on a sharp decomposition theorem for Bergman \(A^1_\alpha\) spaces in tube domains and suggests related problems in other classical settings. Proofs rely on special integral representations, uniform estimates for Bergman spaces, and Forelli-Rudin estimates. The latter section provides basic preliminaries on symmetric cones, including conditions for cones to be open, convex, self-dual, homogeneous, symmetric, and irreducible, and begins recalling determinant-related facts via a Euclidean Jordan algebra framework.
